# Wave W17-AA (Route 221): tide turf — tide-pool coast turf, bog-creep flecks: a walked coast green carrying dark olive bog-creep flecks that thicken toward Fenland’s marsh smoke in the north (design: the Pal coast, where the sea road comes ashore and the marsh begins to breathe over the fence). Route 221’s own ground — split from its twin Route 219 by element entire (the landfall vs the lane that feeds it) and from Route 212-South’s bog turf by degree: this turf is crept on at its edges, that one is bog outright.
